(vector (map (:db/id -1), (:adr/id "adr-2607192200-net-kotobase-commoncrawl-web-search-integration"), (:adr/title "Common Crawl ingestion actor + hybrid web search, extending net-kotobase's existing web.search/web.ingest (real replacement for the retracted ADR-2607081500)"), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/date "2026-07-19"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/topic "net-kotobase-commoncrawl-web-search"), (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "Whether cloud-itonami and net-kotobase have a Google-like whole-web search integrated (answer: not literally arbitrary-keyword whole-web discovery; a growing ingested-and-indexed corpus, see Decision)" "net-kotobase web.ingest/web.search lexicon extension scope (extracted-metadata fields, no new API surface)" "kotoba-lang/kotobase-commoncrawl-actor scope and non-goals" "kotoba-lang/murakumo + gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo embedding engine adapter scope (2026-07-19 addendum: owner approved building it, no longer deferred)")), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607081500 (retracted)" "2607182400-isic-8291-commoncrawl-web-presence-enrichment")), (:adr/supersedes (vector "2607081500-commoncrawl-datom-log-llm-vector-search")), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-19"), (:adr/context (vector "Owner asked whether Google-like whole-web search is integrated into cloud-itonami and net-kotobase; investigation found no such thing, and found that ADR-2607081500 falsely claimed a net-kotobase-commoncrawler resident actor with LLM extraction + vector search was implemented-active, when no such repo, west entry, or GitHub repo ever existed (see that ADR's 2026-07-19 retraction notice)" "net-kotobase already has a real, tested web.ingest/web.search XRPC pair (ai.gftd.apps.kotobase.web.{search,ingest}) — token/Datalog search only, edge explicitly does not crawl, caller must supply url/title/text" "cloud-itonami-isic-8291 already has a real, live-verified dossier.commoncrawl client — Common Crawl's actual Index API is URL-keyed only (no q= full-text/keyword param), so it can verify a known domain's web presence but cannot discover unknown domains by keyword or industry" "kenchi.commoncrawl (kotoba-lang) has a working CDX index-query + WARC-range-fetch pattern for a different domain (real-estate pricing), JVM-only" "No embedding-generation or vector-similarity-search infrastructure exists anywhere in this monorepo: cloud-murakumo exposes chat completions only (api.murakumo.cloud/v1/messages, murakumo-main alias) with no embeddings endpoint; the only real embedding API call found in the whole workspace is an unrelated etzhayyim/yorishiro TypeScript HuggingFace Inference API wrapper; kotoba-lang mst-projector and its etzhayyim scaffold copies are all non-functional Phase-3 stubs (FakeHashEmbedder, throwing LanceDb/DuckDb stubs)" "Owner explicitly ruled out (a) a true unlimited-crawl full web crawler and (b) a thin proxy to an external search API (Google/Bing/etc.) as the design direction, and chose a combination of (1) business-entity-scoped search for cloud-itonami and (2) general Common Crawl bulk ingestion for broader reuse — both of which point at the same real mechanism: an actor that ingests a configurable, growable set of domains via Common Crawl, not an arbitrary-query live web index" "2026-07-19 addendum: owner asked for vector/semantic search to be built now rather than deferred; follow-up investigation of the murakumo fleet found the production text-generation backend is a llama.cpp RPC ring (kotoba-lang/murakumo src/murakumo/infer/engine.cljc, llama-server --rpc across fleet.edn nodes), not Ollama (Ollama appears only in a retired 2026-06 LiteLLM-gateway ADR and personal benchmark notes) — so an Ollama-native /api/embeddings shortcut does not exist in production; gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo's gateway.cljc routing table has zero embeddings route; resources/murakumo.edn has a :batch-embed app entry that is name-and-GPU-reservation only with no :fn/engine and no code path anywhere dispatching to it; a separate, unrelated BGE-M3/Zeebe/RisingWave embedding pipeline exists in ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp for the recruit product but its RisingWave backend is retired (see that repo's CLAUDE.md, RETIRED 2026-06-11), so it is not a live reuse candidate")), (:adr/decision (vector "Retract, do not reimplement, ADR-2607081500's vocabulary: no :db-api abstraction, no langchain-clj (also violates the no--clj-suffix naming rule) — real code uses the existing datomic.q/datomic.transact plane and the kotoba-lang/langchain + kotoba-lang/langgraph + kotoba-lang/langchain-store libraries by their real names" "Define web全体検索 honestly for this workspace: not literal instant arbitrary-keyword discovery across the entire live web (that requires either a self-run full crawler or a third-party search index, both explicitly out of scope) — instead an incrementally-growing corpus ingested from Common Crawl via a seed-domain-list-driven actor, hybrid-searchable (token match today; vector similarity only once real embedding infra exists), seeded first with cloud-itonami business-entity domains and generically extensible to any domain list" "New actor repo kotoba-lang/kotobase-commoncrawl-actor (west-registered, public org, no -clj suffix), structured like gftd-talent-actor: StateGraph nodes intake -> fetch(cc-cdx+warc) -> advise(murakumo-main LLM extraction: category/summary/entities) -> govern -> decide -> commit(calls net-kotobase web.ingest via its own self-minted CACAO identity)/hold; Governor (policy.cljc) hard-blocks domains outside the configured seed list and enforces a per-tick fetch budget; durable outer loop (tick/lease/budget/crash-recovery) driven by a scheduled routine, not an always-on process; own audit ledger via kotoba-lang/langchain-store (not a hand-rolled enc/dec)" "CDX + WARC fetch client written in .cljc/nbb (per repo-wide runtime priority), porting the *lessons* of dossier.commoncrawl (url= is mandatory, real no-match is HTTP 404 + JSON body, not a bare 200) and kenchi.commoncrawl (index-query + ranged WARC fetch shape) — not copying their JVM-only code verbatim" "LLM extraction step follows the 70-tools/bmc llm-complete-fn calling convention (murakumo-main alias resolution, OpenAI/Anthropic dual response parsing, stream default) rather than the unwired cloud_itonami.murakumo GatewayInference client" "Minimal, additive net-kotobase extension: web.ingest gains optional extracted_category/extracted_summary/extracted_entities fields that get folded into the existing tokenized/searchable text (webpage-tx), so the existing, tested web.search benefits immediately with zero new query-side API surface or schema abstraction" "2026-07-19 addendum, vector search approved: self-host, do not take an external embedding API dependency. Add a new llama.cpp-based embedding engine adapter to kotoba-lang/murakumo (sibling to the existing :vllm/:mlx-moe/:llamacpp-rpc adapters in src/murakumo/infer/engine.cljc), running llama-server --embedding --pooling mean on a port separate from the existing chat head so murakumo-main chat traffic is never touched by this change; model is a multilingual embedding GGUF (BGE-M3 class, dense pooling, ~1024-dim) added to infer.edn's :models registry and fetched via the existing generic model_setup.clj downloader (no new download mechanism needed); gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo's gateway.cljc gets one new :serve route (/v1/embeddings) pointing at the new head, deployed only after its own tests pass and confirmed not to alter any existing route's dispatch" "Once the embedding engine is live, net-kotobase's web.ingest computes and stores a :webpage/embedding blob (EDN-encoded float vector) at ingest time by calling the new /v1/embeddings route, and web.search accepts an optional query_embedding to blend token score with cosine similarity against candidates that have one — both additive to the existing schema/API, no candidate loses functionality if it has no embedding yet" "cloud-itonami integration: ISIC actors (starting with isic-8291) call the extended web.search for richer entity web-presence lookups as a complement to, not a replacement for, dossier.commoncrawl's narrower exists/does-not-exist verification")), (:adr/consequences (vector "cloud-itonami and net-kotobase gain a real, deployed, incrementally-growing searchable web corpus instead of a fabricated one, at the honest scope of seed-list-driven Common Crawl ingestion rather than instant arbitrary-keyword whole-web discovery" "Search quality for anything outside the ingested seed domains remains zero until those domains are added to the seed list — this is a config/data-scope limitation, not a code limitation, and must not be described to users as general web search parity with Google" "Semantic/vector search is now in active build (2026-07-19 addendum): the murakumo fleet gains a second, embedding-only llama-server process per participating node, adding GPU/RAM footprint and a new gateway route that must be load-tested to confirm it does not starve or slow the existing chat head before being called production-ready" "The retracted ADR-2607081500 stays in the historical record marked superseded rather than deleted, per this workspace's ADR-supersession convention, so the fabrication and its correction are both auditable" "New actor repo and net-kotobase lexicon change both need west registration / west-pin verification / deploy following the CLAUDE.md-mandated flows (no rebase, no force-push, GitHub API single-entry commits, west-pin-verify guard) before this ADR's decisions are considered fully landed")), (:adr/references (vector "90-docs/adr/2607081500-commoncrawl-datom-log-llm-vector-search.edn (retracted)" "90-docs/adr/2607182400-isic-8291-commoncrawl-web-presence-enrichment.edn" "orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8291/src/dossier/commoncrawl.clj" "orgs/kotoba-lang/kenchi/src/kenchi/commoncrawl.clj" "orgs/gftdcojp/net-kotobase/contracts/lexicons/ai/gftd/apps/kotobase/web/search.json" "orgs/gftdcojp/net-kotobase/contracts/lexicons/ai/gftd/apps/kotobase/web/ingest.json" "orgs/gftdcojp/net-kotobase/clj-edge/src/kotobase/web.cljc" "orgs/gftdcojp/net-kotobase/clj-edge/src/kotobase/domain_search.cljc" "orgs/gftdcojp/net-kotobase/worker/test/web_geo_search_test.cljc" "orgs/gftdcojp/gftd-talent-actor (actor skeleton reference)" "orgs/kotoba-lang/langchain-store" "70-tools/bmc/src/gftd/cli.cljc (llm-complete-fn convention)")), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607192200: Common Crawl ingestion actor + hybrid web search for cloud-itonami / net-kotobase\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-19\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization for new-project scaffold + production deploy)\n**Supersedes**: ADR-2607081500 (retracted — described a resident actor and vector-search stack that was never actually built)\n\n## Context\n\nThe owner asked whether Google-like whole-web search is integrated into cloud-itonami and net-kotobase. Investigation (this session) found:\n\n1. It is not. The only prior evidence pointing the other way, ADR-2607081500, claimed a `net-kotobase-commoncrawler` resident kotoba actor with LLM extraction + vector search was `implemented-active`. That repo does not exist under `orgs/gftdcojp/` or `orgs/kotoba-lang/`, is not registered in `manifest/repos.edn`/`west.yml`, and returns 404 on GitHub for every plausible owner. That ADR has been retracted (status changed to `superseded`, retraction notice appended to its body) rather than silently deleted, so the fabrication stays auditable.\n2. Real, working infrastructure already exists and is the correct extension point:\n   - `net-kotobase`'s `ai.gftd.apps.kotobase.web.search` / `web.ingest` XRPC pair is implemented and tested (`clj-edge/src/kotobase/{web,domain_search}.cljc`, `worker/test/web_geo_search_test.cljc`). It does token/Datalog search only; the edge explicitly does not crawl — callers supply already-extracted `url`/`title`/`text`.\n   - `cloud-itonami-isic-8291`'s `dossier.commoncrawl` is a real, live-verified Common Crawl Index API client. It proved (and fixed, live) that CC's Index API is strictly URL-keyed — there is no keyword/industry discovery parameter — and that a genuine no-match is HTTP 404 with a JSON body, not a bare 200. It deliberately stays out of the governed `dossier.facts` company registry: a URL existing is not proof of a registered legal entity.\n   - `kenchi.commoncrawl` (kotoba-lang) has a working, different-domain (real-estate pricing) CDX-query + ranged-WARC-fetch pattern, JVM-only.\n   - No embedding-generation or vector-similarity infrastructure exists anywhere in this monorepo. `cloud-murakumo` exposes chat completions only. The only real embedding API call in the whole workspace is an unrelated etzhayyim/yorishiro TypeScript wrapper around the HuggingFace Inference API. `kotoba-lang/mst-projector` and its many etzhayyim actor-scaffold copies are non-functional Phase-3 stubs (`FakeHashEmbedder`, `throw`-ing LanceDB/DuckDB adapters).\n3. The owner, given the choice between a true unlimited crawler, an external search-API proxy, business-entity-scoped search, and general Common-Crawl-based ingestion, ruled out the first two and chose the latter two together. Both point at the same real, buildable mechanism: an actor that ingests a configurable, growable list of domains via Common Crawl — not a live arbitrary-keyword index of the entire web (which is infeasible on this fleet and was explicitly rejected).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Retract ADR-2607081500's vocabulary entirely.** No `:db-api` abstraction, no `langchain-clj` naming (violates the no-`-clj`-suffix rule). Real code talks to `datomic.q`/`datomic.transact` and to the real library names (`kotoba-lang/langchain`, `kotoba-lang/langgraph`, `kotoba-lang/langchain-store`).\n2. **Define \"web全体検索\" honestly.** Not literal instant arbitrary-keyword discovery across the entire live web. Instead: an incrementally-growing corpus ingested from Common Crawl via a seed-domain-list-driven actor, hybrid-searchable (token match today; vector similarity only once real embedding infrastructure exists and an owner decision funds/builds it), seeded first with cloud-itonami business-entity domains and generically extensible to any additional domain list over time.\n3. **New actor repo `kotoba-lang/kotobase-commoncrawl-actor`** (west-registered, public org per `repos.edn :orgs :visibility`), structured like `gftd-talent-actor`:\n   - StateGraph: `intake -> fetch(cc-cdx+warc) -> advise(murakumo-main LLM extraction: category/summary/entities) -> govern -> decide -> commit(web.ingest via self-minted CACAO)/hold`.\n   - Governor (`policy.cljc`): hard-blocks any domain outside the configured seed list, enforces a per-tick fetch budget, hard-blocks disallowed content categories.\n   - Durable outer loop (tick/lease/budget/crash-recovery), driven by a scheduled routine rather than an always-on process.\n   - Own audit ledger via `kotoba-lang/langchain-store` (not a 191st hand-rolled `enc`/`dec*`).\n4. **CDX + WARC client in `.cljc`/nbb** (per repo-wide runtime priority — kotoba wasm > clojurewasm > cljs > nbb > jvm/bb), porting the *lessons* of `dossier.commoncrawl` (mandatory `url=`, real no-match is 404+JSON) and `kenchi.commoncrawl` (index-query + ranged WARC fetch shape) rather than copying their JVM-only code.\n5. **LLM extraction follows the `70-tools/bmc` `llm-complete-fn` convention** (`murakumo-main` alias resolution, dual OpenAI/Anthropic response parsing, stream default) — not the unwired `cloud_itonami.murakumo` `GatewayInference` client, which its own docstring says has zero callers and should not be wired yet.\n6. **Minimal, additive net-kotobase extension.** `web.ingest` gains optional `extracted_category`/`extracted_summary`/`extracted_entities` fields, folded into the existing tokenized/searchable text (`webpage-tx`). The existing, tested `web.search` benefits immediately with zero new query-side API surface.\n7. **Vector/semantic search is explicitly out of scope for this pass** and must not be claimed as done. It needs a real embedding-serving decision (self-host on the murakumo fleet vs. a new external paid dependency) that has cost/ownership implications an implementation pass should not decide unilaterally. Tracked as an open follow-up.\n8. **cloud-itonami integration**: ISIC actors (starting with isic-8291) call the extended `web.search` for richer entity web-presence lookups, complementing rather than replacing `dossier.commoncrawl`'s narrower exists/does-not-exist verification.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- cloud-itonami and net-kotobase gain a real, deployed, incrementally-growing searchable web corpus instead of a fabricated one — honestly scoped as seed-list-driven Common Crawl ingestion, not instant arbitrary-keyword whole-web discovery.\n- Search quality outside the ingested seed domains is zero until those domains are added — a config/data-scope limitation, not a code limitation, and must never be described as Google-parity general web search.\n- Semantic/vector search stays unavailable until a follow-up ADR makes an explicit embedding-infra decision with owner input.\n- ADR-2607081500 remains in the historical record, marked `superseded`, so the fabrication and its correction are both auditable — it was not deleted.\n- The new actor repo and the net-kotobase lexicon change both need west registration / west-pin verification / production deploy following the CLAUDE.md-mandated flows before this ADR's decisions are fully landed.\n\n## References\n\n- `90-docs/adr/2607081500-commoncrawl-datom-log-llm-vector-search.edn` (retracted)\n- `90-docs/adr/2607182400-isic-8291-commoncrawl-web-presence-enrichment.edn`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8291/src/dossier/commoncrawl.clj`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/kenchi/src/kenchi/commoncrawl.clj`\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/net-kotobase/contracts/lexicons/ai/gftd/apps/kotobase/web/{search,ingest}.json`\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/net-kotobase/clj-edge/src/kotobase/{web,domain_search}.cljc`\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/net-kotobase/worker/test/web_geo_search_test.cljc`\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/gftd-talent-actor` (actor skeleton reference)\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/langchain-store`\n- `70-tools/bmc/src/gftd/cli.cljc` (`llm-complete-fn` convention)\n\n## 2026-07-19 Addendum: vector/semantic search approved, self-hosted on the murakumo fleet\n\nThe owner asked for vector/semantic search to be built now instead of staying deferred. Investigation of `kotoba-lang/murakumo` + `gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo` found:\n\n- The production text-generation backend is a **llama.cpp RPC ring** (`src/murakumo/infer/engine.cljc`, `llama-server --rpc` across the nodes in `fleet.edn`), not Ollama. Ollama only appears in a retired 2026-06 LiteLLM-gateway ADR and personal benchmark notes — an `/api/embeddings` shortcut does not exist in the current production path.\n- `gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo`'s `gateway.cljc` routing table has zero embeddings route today.\n- `resources/murakumo.edn` has a `:batch-embed` app entry, but it is name-and-GPU-reservation only — no `:fn/engine`, no code anywhere dispatches to it.\n- A separate BGE-M3/Zeebe/RisingWave embedding pipeline exists in `ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp` for the unrelated recruit product, but its RisingWave storage backend is retired (2026-06-11) — not a live reuse candidate.\n\n**Decision**: self-host, do not take a new external embedding API dependency. Add a new embedding engine adapter to `kotoba-lang/murakumo`, sibling to the existing `:vllm`/`:mlx-moe`/`:llamacpp-rpc` adapters — `llama-server --embedding --pooling mean` on a **separate port** from the existing chat head, so `murakumo-main` chat traffic is never touched. Model: a multilingual BGE-M3-class GGUF (~1024-dim dense pooling), added to `infer.edn`'s `:models` registry, fetched via the existing generic `model_setup.clj` downloader. `cloud-murakumo`'s `gateway.cljc` gets one new `:serve` route, `/v1/embeddings`, deployed only after its own tests pass and after confirming it does not alter any existing route's dispatch (a routing-table-only, additive change).\n\nOnce live, `net-kotobase`'s `web.ingest` computes and stores a `:webpage/embedding` blob at ingest time via this route, and `web.search` accepts an optional `query_embedding` to blend token score with cosine similarity — both additive; candidates without an embedding yet keep working exactly as before.\n\nThis is real new GPU/RAM footprint on a shared production fleet serving other consumers (see CLAUDE.md's `murakumo-main` repo-wide mandatory section) — the embedding head must be load-tested to confirm it does not degrade the existing chat head before being called production-ready, not just \"deployed\".")))
